# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — THE ONE RULE THAT MATTERS HERE
#
# NEVER commit an API token, an account ID, or a CRN to this repository.
# This project talks to real quantum hardware, so a leaked token is a leaked
# billable resource tied to a real account. Concretely:
#
#   * tokens are read from the environment ONLY (IBM_QUANTUM_API_TOKEN, or the
#     QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN alternative), and `python/tkr_ibm.py` never writes them
#     to disk;
#   * `config/.env.template` IS safe to commit because it holds placeholders
#     only ("your_api_key_here" style values), never a working credential —
#     it is the file you copy to `config/.env`, and `config/.env` is ignored
#     below;
#   * if you ever need to share a run, export the variables in your shell or
#     redact the value; never paste a token into a log, a report, or a doc.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local secret files. `.env.*` would also swallow the template, so the
# template is explicitly re-included right after it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.template
!config/.env.template

# Python bytecode / caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Packaging and build output
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
wheels/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Local distribution-build scratch directory (holds the .whl/.tar.gz used to
# verify MANIFEST.in before tagging a release — machine-specific, never tracked)
_distcheck/

# arXiv submission bundle (generated by `make arxiv-bundle` or the documented
# tar command; contains a copy of the paper sources, not the repo itself)
arxiv-bundle/
arxiv/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Test / lint / type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Rust build output (the compiled crate is rebuilt from rust/, never committed;
# rust/target is multi-gigabyte and machine-specific)
rust/target/
target/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Measurement output that may embed run metadata
*.qasm